 "description": "Playable Sinaloa game area from real data, about 16 x 17 km: the Culiacan region (lagoon and mangroves, the irrigated valley, the capital at 1:2, the foothills and the reservoir) and the Mazatlan region (the port city at 1:2 with its islands, port and cruise piers, the hills, Sierra and Presidio plain) laid along one coast at 1:6 across and 1:3 up, eroded; the cities end where their built-up land does. Elevation Copernicus 30 m, OSM via Overpass, WorldCover land cover, GEBCO bathymetry through OpenTopography (free API key). Generated by scratch-look/py/spec.py: positions come from real latitudes and longitudes. worldBuild(file='sinaloa_real.json', estimate=True) lists missing downloads; worldBuild(file='sinaloa_real.json', fetch=True, consent=True, replace=True) fetches them into real/ and builds (about 6 minutes, 35 GB peak). Regional building styles come from the BuildingStyles folder.",
